red  phrase i see them in uh you know on the  face of the flash card and i'll just go  through them very quickly it's just  exposure i don't try to force myself to  think  um  you know i don't like i do review  grammar but again not with the objective  that i'm going to learn it it's just  exposure just like the flashcard is  exposure but most of my time i spend  doing interesting things  um so yeah i'm lazy i won't go to class  um what else don't i like to do  what else is there answer questions  um  yeah because i know like also  so i like to read things of interest but  i will also review beginner material and  this is another thing when i start into  my beginner books teach yourself or  whatever it might be or beginner lessons  at link i know that i'll be back at  those in you know in a month in three  months in six months and it'll be easier  every time so i'm not  concerned about mastering anything i  don't try to memorize tables i'm too  lazy to try to memorize tables  i don't read out loud i don't  learn the international phonetic  alphabet i i don't never use it  i just listen  uh and i at first the car the  pronunciation is difficult and there's  things that i miss at first and then i  get later on there's always this idea  that we aren't going to notice things  the first time around when we'll notice  them later on so i'm quite comfortable  to just let it go  i jump around  from more difficult to less difficult  different material  and i just i just do whatever the spirit  sort of  wherever the spirit moves me that's  where i go um  so in that sense i'm a lazy  language learner i'm not a disciplined  language learner i won't do these i  don't do shadowing for example i won't  go out there and deliberately learn 100  phrases or 300 sentences or or whatever  it is  um  i like to review phrases specifically  you know patterns of different or  examples of different patterns in the  language all of that is is just a  process of of exposure  so that eventually 